rsx vp decompiler: BRB/CLB branch on the transform branch bits; block leaders up to slot 544.

Resistance 3 draws its glows and light shafts with one 543-slot vertex program that picks its optional paths with 21
"BRB !bN" branches on SET_TRANSFORM_BRANCH_BITS (0x1004, 0x1001, 0x1008, ... per draw). Two things kept it off
screen:
- the leader table stopped at slot 512 of the 544-slot transform memory, so past it no block was opened, every later
  branch closed a block that was never opened and main() ended early ("function does not return a value: @main");
  every draw using the program (four fragment programs in the Home level) was dropped;
- BRB/CLB were "not modelled" and fell through, so with the first fix alone every optional path ran and the effects
  came out as red stretched polygons around Susan.
A boolean branch now tests bit D3[23:27] of the branch bits against D3[28] (RPCS3's GetOptionalBranchCond; the CC
condition does not apply). The outcome is baked into the program, so the engine and live_draw read the register
(0x1FF8) and key the pipeline on it, only for programs that use BRB/CLB (rsx_vp_uses_branch_bits).

test_shader_msl: a 519-slot program with BRIs past slot 512 gets its blocks (three checks fail without the leader
change); BRB !b3 and CLB b12 take or skip their targets for two sets of bits and translate to MSL.
Scripted run (Home level): no pipeline failures; the program's ~90 draws a frame in the effects pass are back (the
glow and light shaft of Susan's lantern and the room lamps), no red polygons.

Upstream: PR #485. Kept on top of upstream/pr459 (the hash line moved to eng_vp_hash).

